    "problem_statement": "mq_unlink() reports the wrong error when asked to remove a named message queue that does not exist. Per POSIX, calling mq_unlink() with the name of a non-existent message queue must return -1 and set errno to ENOENT, but instead it sets errno to EBADF (a code reserved for invalid file descriptors). A caller checking errno after a failed mq_unlink() therefore sees the wrong error for the 'queue not found' case.",
